# A `for` row's entry is a projection of its source (Semantics ch. 4): `$_` (here `$v`) is
# `$items[k]`, a dynamic derived from the block's holds, read at the row's read point and
# written by nobody. So `!Updated $v` is the entry's event half: it fires in the tick a block
# hold behind the source moves, at its height above that hold's writer, with the entry after
# the tick; the label over `$v` and the count of its updates move in the same tick. The
# event fires whenever the source is recomputed, deduped by nobody (pick UD): an edit of key
# 0 counts in row 1 too. A row reading a block hold through its parent has the same event
# half: `!Updated $twice`, over `$edits`, fires in the tick of the edit. A key that leaves
# ends its row at the end of that tick (R8); the row's label is read in the leaving tick,
# after its key is gone, and reads its last value. Written for prismc's back end. Work in
# progress, subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@entries: @unit
@entries:
    !add <- Ui.Button(label=$"add")                                        # 0
    !edit <- Ui.Button(label=$"edit")                                      # 1
    !drop <- Ui.Button(label=$"drop")                                      # 2
    $next <- 1 then $next + 1 on !add
    $edits <- 0 then $edits + 1 on !edit
    $items <- {0: "a"} then (Insert $items, $next, "b{$next}") on !add <| (Insert $items, 0, "e{$edits}") on !edit <| (Remove $items, 0) on !drop
    for k, $v <- $items:                                                   # 3/[k]
        $n <- 0 then $n + 1 on (!Updated $v)
        let $twice = $edits * 2
        $m <- 0 then $m + 1 on (!Updated $twice)
        Ui.Label(text=$"{k}: {$v} changed {$n}, edits {$m}")               # 3/[k]/0
